  parkRegs:"Native Trout Conservation Area: all native fish — cutthroat, mountain whitefish, Arctic grayling — go back unharmed, and there is no possession limit on nonnative fish. In the Lamar drainage, which is this river and every tributary and lake in it, <b>all rainbow trout, brook trout and identifiable cutthroat × rainbow hybrids must be killed</b> — releasing one alive is illegal.",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"The Lamar Valley's river — out of the Absaroka backcountry, through the cottonwood flats where the bison and the wolf-watchers are, to the Yellowstone at Tower Junction. Silty and unfishable through runoff, then one of the great dry-fly rivers of the Rockies from July on.",
