  parkRegsSrc:"colorado",
  parkRegs:"<i>Gold Medal Water</i> — From the confluence with the Lake Fork of the Arkansas near Leadville downstream to Parkdale at the U.S. 50 bridge crossing above the Royal Gorge.<br><br><b>Within the Pueblo Reservoir State Wildlife Area:</b><br>• Bag, possession and min. size for walleye and saugeye is 5 in the aggregate, 18 inches long.<br>• Only 1 walleye or saugeye in the aggregate longer than 21 inches may be taken per day.<br><b>From the bridge at Valco Ponds downstream to Pueblo Blvd. (except at Pueblo Nature Center, as posted):</b><br>• Artificial flies and lures only.<br>• Trout longer than 16 inches must be returned to water immediately.<br><br><b>Colorado statewide limits</b> — trout, arctic char, grayling, salmon and mountain whitefish (except kokanee), in aggregate: 4 daily bag, 8 possession; trout include brook, brown, cutbow, cutthroat, golden, lake, rainbow, splake and tiger trout. Brook trout 8 inches long or less: 10 daily, 10 possession, in addition to the trout limit. Greenback cutthroat trout may not be taken and must be returned to the water immediately.",
