  parkRegs:"All harvested fish caught in the Bartlett River must be kept within six feet of the angler or on their person, and packed out whole, except gills and entrails, which should be deposited in the deepest, fastest-flowing part of the stream channel. An <b>Alaska sportfishing licence</b> is required for all nonresidents 16 and older and for Alaska residents 18–59. In fresh water, NPS regulations allow hook and line gear only and prohibit live or dead bait, unpreserved fish eggs or roe, and chumming. Fish that don't meet size or species restrictions must be carefully and immediately released.<br><br>Everything not covered above falls under the <b>Southeast fresh water general regulations</b> — ADF&amp;G 2026 Southeast booklet, p. 10.",
