  parkRegsSrc:"alaska",
  parkRegs:"<b>DEEP CREEK DRAINAGE:</b><br>• January 1-July 15: Closed to all sport fishing. King salmon: King salmon fishing is closed in 2026 by emergency order.<br>• Rainbow/steelhead trout: Catch-and-release fishing only. All rainbow/steelhead trout caught may not be removed from the water and must be released immediately.<br>• Other species: See general regulations on pages 60-61.<br><b>From its mouth upstream approximately 2 miles to ADF&amp;G markers:</b><br>• See the table on the right for open dates and gear allowed in this area.<br><b>Upstream from ADF&amp;G markers:</b><br>• Closed year-round to all salmon fishing.<br>• November 1-July 31: Closed to all sport fishing in flowing waters.<br>• August 1-October 31: Open to sport fishing for species other than salmon.<br>• Only one unbaited, single-hook artificial lure or fly is allowed.<br><i>— ADF&amp;G 2026 Southcentral regulations, p. 63</i><br><br>Everything not covered above falls under the <b>Kenai Peninsula general regulations</b> — ADF&amp;G 2026 Southcentral booklet, p. 60.",
