  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  parkRegsSrc:"alaska",
  parkRegs:"<b>CHATANIKA RIVER DRAINAGE:</b><br>• Open year-round to sport fishing for species other than northern pike. April 15-October 14: Open to northern pike fishing. Whitefish may not be taken by a spear or bow and arrow. Please contact the ADF&amp;G Fairbanks office for information on the Chatanika River personal use whitefish spear fishery. For sport fishing (hook and line) whitefish limits, see page 20.<br>• Only unbaited, artificial lures or flies may be used, except that bait may be used only on hooks with a gap between point and shank larger than ¾ inch.<br>• Upstream from the mouth of Goldstream Creek to the boundary of the Fairbanks Nonsubsistence Use area (identified by an ADF&amp;G marker located approximately 1 mile downstream of the Murphy Dome Road):<br>• Only single-hooks may be used.<br><b>Upstream of the upstream edge of the Elliott Highway bridge:</b><br>• Closed to all salmon fishing. All salmon caught must be released immediately.<br><i>— ADF&amp;G 2026 Northern regulations, p. 21</i><br><br>Everything not covered above falls under the <b>Tanana general regulations</b> — ADF&amp;G 2026 Northern booklet, p. 20.",
