  id:"beaverhead", name:"Beaverhead River", color:"#a8552a",
  state:"MT", region:"montana", gauges:["beaverheadBarretts","beaverheadDillon","beaverheadTwinBridges","beaverheadTwinBridges2"], primaryGauge:"beaverheadTwinBridges",
  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  parkRegsSrc:"montana",
  parkRegs:"<b>Entire river</b><br>• Rainbow trout: Catch-and-release only.<br><b>Clark Canyon Dam to Pipe Organ Bridge</b><br>• Open third Saturday in May through Sept. 30.<br><b>Clark Canyon Dam to High Bridge FAS</b><br>• Catch-and-release for brown trout.<br>• Artificial lures and single-pointed hooks only. Anglers may remove treble or double hooks from the lure and replace them with a single hook, or the shanks may be cut off the other hook points to leave a single hook. Lures with multiple hook attachments may still be used but any treble hook must be replaced by a single hook.<br><b>Barretts Diversion to the Mouth</b><br>• Open April 1 through Sept. 30.<br>• Brown trout: Catch-and-release only.<br><b>High Bridge to Barretts Diversion</b><br>• Brown trout: 5 fish daily and in possession. All fish must be less than 18”.<br><b>Recreation Rules High Bridge FAS to Henneberry FAS</b><br>• Closed to float fishing by nonresidents and float outfitting on each Saturday from the third Saturday in May through Labor Day.<br><br><b>Central District standard rules</b> — rivers and streams open all year. Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden and cutthroat trout and arctic grayling): 3 daily and in possession, only 1 over 18 inches, only 1 can be a cutthroat trout; all arctic grayling must be released immediately. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession.",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
