  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  parkRegsSrc:"montana",
  parkRegs:"<b>From the confluence of the Middle and West forks, near Philipsburg, to the mouth</b><br>• Combined trout: 3 brown trout daily and in possession. Catch-and- release for rainbow trout and cutthroat trout.<br>• Artificial lures only, except anglers 14 years of age or younger may use bait during the general season.<br>• Closed to fishing from boats/vessels July 1 through Nov. 30.<br>• Extended season for whitefish and catch-and-release for trout open Dec. 1 to third Saturday in May with artificial lures and/or maggots only.<br><br><b>Western District standard rules</b> — rivers and streams open the third Saturday in May through Nov. 30. Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden trout and arctic grayling): 3 daily and in possession, only 1 over 14 inches. Cutthroat trout: 3 daily and in possession, none over 12 inches. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession. All waters are closed to angling for bull trout, and all must be released without delay.",
