  parkRegsSrc:"montana",
  parkRegs:"• Catch-and-release for cutthroat trout and rainbow trout.<br>• Brown trout: 3 daily and in possession.<br>• Extended season for northern pike and whitefish and catch-and- release for trout from Dec. 1 to third Saturday in May with aquatic insects, maggots and/or artificial lures only.<br><b>Recreation Rules (see fwp.mt.gov/recreation/permits/floating/ and signs on site for more information) West Fork Bitterroot River and Upper Bitterroot River (see map page 25) No commercial floating or fishing June 1 to Sept. 15 from</b><br>• Painted Rocks Dam to Applebury Forest Service Site on Fridays.<br>• Applebury Forest Service Site to Trapper Creek Job Corps Site on Saturdays.<br>• Trapper Creek Job Corps Site on to Hannon Memorial FAS on Sundays.<br>• Hannon Memorial FAS to Wally Crawford FAS on Mondays.<br><b>No floating of any kind July 1 to Sept. 15 from</b><br>• Painted Rocks Dam to Applebury Forest Service Site on Fridays.<br><br><b>Western District standard rules</b> — rivers and streams open the third Saturday in May through Nov. 30. Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden trout and arctic grayling): 3 daily and in possession, only 1 over 14 inches. Cutthroat trout: 3 daily and in possession, none over 12 inches. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession. All waters are closed to angling for bull trout, and all must be released without delay.",
