  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  parkRegsSrc:"montana",
  parkRegs:"<b>Clearwater River upstream from the Salmon Lake inlet and all tributaries of the Clearwater River except the West Fork and Marshall Creek</b><br>• Closed to fishing from Rainey Lake fish barrier downstream for 100 yards.<br>• Catch-and-release for cutthroat trout.<br>• Northern pike: no limit.<br>• Snagging: open for kokanee salmon from Lake Alva outlet to Lake Inez inlet and from Lake Inez outlet to Seeley Lake inlet from Sept. 15 through Nov. 30. Closed to snagging from Seeley Lake outlet to Salmon Lake inlet.<br><i>NOTE: Clearwater River sections between lakes are closed to fishing from Dec. 1 until the third Saturday in May. This includes the Clearwater River section from outlet of Seeley Lake at Riverview Drive Bridge (“Dogtown”) downstream to inlet of Salmon Lake.</i><br><b>Clearwater River from Salmon Lake outlet to mouth of the Clearwater River, including Blanchard Lake and Elbow Lake</b><br>• Open entire year.<br>• Catch-and-release for cutthroat trout.<br>• Combined trout: 3 daily and in possession, Only 1 rainbow trout over 14 inches.<br>• Northern pike: no limit.<br><br><b>Western District standard rules</b> — rivers and streams open the third Saturday in May through Nov. 30. Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden trout and arctic grayling): 3 daily and in possession, only 1 over 14 inches. Cutthroat trout: 3 daily and in possession, none over 12 inches. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession. All waters are closed to angling for bull trout, and all must be released without delay.",
