  id:"smithmt", name:"Smith River (MT)", color:"#4f8f6f",
  state:"MT", region:"montana", gauges:["smithFtLogan","smithEagleCr","smithEden"], primaryGauge:"smithEagleCr",
  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  parkRegsSrc:"montana",
  parkRegs:"<i>NOTE: Floating on the Smith River between Camp Baker and Eden Bridge is strictly limited. Mandatory registration, floater’s fee and other regulations apply. A drawing for launch dates is held in February with remaining launches filled on a first-come basis. Contact the Great Falls FWP office at 406-454-5840 for more information.</i><br><b>Sheep Creek from bridge upstream of Moose Creek to the mouth, Rock Creek from bridge at Lingshire Road to the mouth, Tenderfoot Creek from falls just upstream of Daisy Creek to the mouth, and Hound Creek from Upper Millegan Road bridge to the mouth.</b><br>• Open third Saturday in May to Nov. 30.<br><b>Camp Baker Bridge to Eden Bridge</b><br>• Combined trout: 3 under 13 inches daily and in possession and only 1 over 22 inches daily and in possession.<br>• Artificial lures only, except anglers 14 years of age or younger may use bait.<br><br><b>Central District standard rules</b> — rivers and streams open all year. Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden and cutthroat trout and arctic grayling): 3 daily and in possession, only 1 over 18 inches, only 1 can be a cutthroat trout; all arctic grayling must be released immediately. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession.",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
