  parkRegsSrc:"montana",
  parkRegs:"<b>Entire River</b><br>• Smallmouth bass: All smallmouth bass caught must be killed immediately, kept and the entire fish presented to FWP. Anglers who catch smallmouth bass in the Shields River are required to report the catch to FWP within 24 hours (406-577-7900). Anglers will be asked to provide location, date, and time of capture and may be asked to provide their full name, ALS number, and phone number. Anglers are required to present the whole smallmouth bass to a FWP office within 10 days of capture (frozen is allowed) during regular business hours. Edible portions of the fish are returned to the angler upon request.<br><br><b>Central District standard rules</b> — rivers and streams open all year. Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden and cutthroat trout and arctic grayling): 3 daily and in possession, only 1 over 18 inches, only 1 can be a cutthroat trout; all arctic grayling must be released immediately. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession.",
