  id:"flatheadmt", name:"Flathead River (Columbia Falls to Flathead Lake)", color:"#5b8c2a",
  state:"MT", region:"montana", gauges:["flatheadColumbiaFalls"], primaryGauge:"flatheadColumbiaFalls",
  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  parkRegsSrc:"montana",
  parkRegs:"<b>From the confluence of North and Middle Forks to Flathead Lake</b><br>• Hooks/lures must have single points, no double or treble hooks.<br>• Open entire year.<br>• Catch-and-release for cutthroat trout.<br>• Rainbow trout: 5 daily and in possession.<br>• From Dec. 1 to third Saturday in May, maggots and artificial lures only, no artificial lures can be scented (infused, saturated, or applied).<br><br><b>Western District standard rules</b> — rivers and streams open the third Saturday in May through Nov. 30. Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden trout and arctic grayling): 3 daily and in possession, only 1 over 14 inches. Cutthroat trout: 3 daily and in possession, none over 12 inches. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession. All waters are closed to angling for bull trout, and all must be released without delay.",
