  parkRegs:"<b>Owens River (Inyo and Mono cos.), except (A), (B), (C), and (D) below.</b><br>• All year. <i>Bag: 5 trout</i><br><b>Upper Owens River from Benton Bridge road crossing upstream to Big Springs. Above Big Springs, see Deadman Creek (subsection 7.50(b)(41)).</b><br>• All year. Only artificial lures with barbless hooks may be used. <i>Bag: 0 trout</i><br><b>Upper Owens River from Benton Bridge road crossing to Crowley Lake.</b><br>• Last Sat. in Apr. through Jul. 31. <i>Bag: 5 trout</i><br>• Aug. 1 through Nov. 15. Only artificial lures may be used. Minimum size limit: 18 inches total length. <i>Bag: 2 trout</i><br><b>From Pleasant Valley Dam downstream to footbridge at lower end of Pleasant Valley Campground.</b><br>• Last Sat. in Apr. through Nov. 15. <i>Bag: 2 trout. 4 trout in possession.</i><br>• Nov. 16 through the Fri. preceding the last Sat. in Apr. Only artificial lures with barbless hooks may be used. <i>Bag: 0 trout</i><br><b>From footbridge at lower end of Pleasant Valley Campground east (downstream) to 5 Bridges Road.</b><br>• All year. Only artificial lures with barbless hooks may be used. <i>Bag: 0 trout</i><br><br><b>California statewide stream rule</b> (§5.85) — open the last Saturday in April through November 15 with a five-trout daily bag and ten-trout possession limit, no gear restrictions. From November 16 through the Friday preceding the last Saturday in April, a zero-trout bag limit applies and only artificial lures with barbless hooks may be used; trout must be released unharmed and should not be removed from the water.",
