  parkRegsSrc:"california",
  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 7 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>Kings River (Fresno Co.). </b><br><b>Kings River, South Fork from its confluence with Copper Creek downstream to the Highway 180 crossing at Boyden Cave.</b><br>• All year. <i>Bag: 2 trout. 4 trout in possession.</i><br><b>Kings River South Fork, from the Highway 180 crossing at Boyden Cave downstream to the main stem; Middle Fork, from the western boundary of Kings Canyon National Park downstream to the main stem; and main stem, from the confluence of the South and Middle forks downstream to Garnet Dike Campground.</b><br>• All year. Only artificial lures with barbless hooks may be used. <i>Bag: 0 trout</i><br><b>Kings River, from Garnet Dike Campground downstream to Pine Flat Lake.</b><br>• All year. <i>Bag: 2 trout. 4 trout in possession.</i><br><b>Kings River from Pine Flat Dam downstream to U. S. Army Corps of Engineers Bridge on Pine Flat Road. (E)1. Kings River from the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers Bridge on Pine Flat Road downstream to Cobbles (Alta) Weir. (E)2. Kings River Thorburn Spawning Channel, the 2,200 foot long channel located 5 miles downstream from Pine Flat Dam, and the reach of river within a 200-foot radius of the channel exit.</b><br>• Closed to all fishing all year.<br>• All year. <i>Bag: 5 trout</i><br>• Closed to all fishing all year.<br><b>Kings River from Cobbles (Alta) Weir downstream to the Highway 180 crossing.</b><br>• All year. Only artificial lures with barbless hooks may be used. <i>Bag: 0 trout</i><br><b>Kings River from the Highway 180 crossing downstream. Body of Water</b><br>• All year. <i>Bag: 5 trout</i><br>• Open Season and Special Restrictions <i>Bag: Daily Bag and Possession Limit</i></details><br><br><b>California statewide stream rule</b> (§5.85) — open the last Saturday in April through November 15 with a five-trout daily bag and ten-trout possession limit, no gear restrictions. From November 16 through the Friday preceding the last Saturday in April, a zero-trout bag limit applies and only artificial lures with barbless hooks may be used; trout must be released unharmed and should not be removed from the water.",
