  parkRegs:"<b>From the tips of the jetties to the confluence of the East and West Fork Hood River</b><br>• Catch-and-release for trout.<br>• Open for hatchery Chinook salmon from Apr 15 - Jun 30. Daily limit is 1 adult hatchery spring Chinook salmon per day.<br>• Open all year for hatchery coho salmon and hatchery steelhead.<br>• Use of bait allowed for salmon and steelhead.<br><br><b>Central Zone standard rules</b> — streams open May 22 – Oct 31 unless noted under Exceptions. 2 trout per day, 3 daily limits in possession, 8 inch minimum length, only 1 trout over 20 inches per day. Angling restricted to artificial flies and lures in streams unless an exception allows bait. Rainbow trout over 20 inches are considered steelhead in streams.",
