  parkRegs:"<b>from mouth to Hwy. 9 Bridge</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: CLOSED WATERS.<br><b>from Hwy. 9 to Maple Creek CRC (790)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Oct. 1-Nov. 30 Night closure. Anti-snagging rule. Nov. 1-Nov. 30 Motors prohibited.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Oct. 1-Nov. 30 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\".<br>• <b>Steelhead</b>: (hatchery) Oct. 1-Nov. 30 Closed.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Oct. 1-Nov. 30 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Oct. 1-Oct. 15 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 wild coho and no more than 2 hatchery Chinook. Release chum and wild Chinook. Oct. 16-Nov. 30 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 wild coho and no more than 2 Chinook . Release chum.<br><b>from Maple Creek to Nooksack Falls CRC (790)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Selective gear rules. Nov. 1-Nov. 30 Motors prohibited.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Oct. 1-Nov. 30 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\".<br>• <b>Steelhead</b>: Oct. 1-Nov. 30 Closed.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Oct. 1-Nov. 30 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.<br><br><i>Selective gear rules</i>: artificial flies or lures with barbless single-point hooks only, bait prohibited, up to 3 hooks, knotless nets only.",
