  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 17 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>from mouth (a line projected from the James River pumphouse across the Wash- ougal River to the east end of the Hwy. 14 Bridge) to the boat ramp at the WDFW County Line Access Site CRC (667)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older). Night closure. Apr. 16-Fri. before Memorial Day Selective gear rules, except barbed hooks are allowed. Year-round CLOSED WATERS - from 1,000’ (or posted markers)<br><b>below to 200’ above the temporary weir when the weir is installed in the river. July 1-Oct. 31 Anti-snagging rule.</b><br>• <b>All game fish</b>: Mar. 16-Apr. 15 Closed.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Apr. 16-Fri. before Memorial Day Catch-and-release. Sat. before Memorial Day-Mar. 15 Min. size 14”. Daily limit 2.<br>• <b>Steelhead</b>: (hatchery) Apr. 16-Mar. 15 Min. size 20”. Daily limit 3.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Apr. 16-Mar. 15 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Aug. 1-Dec. 31 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6. Up to 3 adults including no more than 2 Chinook may be retained. Release all salmon other than hatchery Chinook and hatchery coho.<br><b>from the boat ramp at the WDFW County Line Access Site to the bridge at Salmon Falls CRC (668)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older). Year-round CLOSED WATERS - from 1,000’ (or posted markers)<br><b>below to 200’ above the temporary weir when the weir is installed in the river. Aug. 1-Oct. 31 Anti-snagging rule. Night closure.</b><br>• <b>Trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Mar. 15 Min. size 14”. Daily limit 2.<br>• <b>Steelhead</b>: (hatchery) Sat. before Memorial Day-Mar. 15 Min. size 20”. Daily limit 3.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Mar. 15 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Aug. 1-Dec. 31 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6. Up to 3 adults including no more than 2 Chinook may be retained. Release all salmon other than hatchery Chinook and hatchery coho.<br><b>from the bridge at Salmon Falls upstream</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: CLOSED WATERS. SPECIES DATE ADDITIONAL RULES</details><br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.<br><br><i>Selective gear rules</i>: artificial flies or lures with barbless single-point hooks only, bait prohibited, up to 3 hooks, knotless nets only.",
