  parkRegsSrc:"washington",
  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 12 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>from mouth (BNSF Railroad Bridge) to County Rd. Bridge below the former location of the powerhouse CRC (508)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older). July 1-Oct. 31 Night closure for salmon and steelhead fishing only. Aug. 1-Dec. 31 Anti-snagging rule.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Year-round Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Release wild cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Year-round Statewide min. size/daily limit. Salmon and hatchery<br>• <b>steelhead</b>: Apr. 1-June 30 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 2 salmon or 2 hatchery steelhead or 1 of each. Release wild Chinook. July 1-July 31 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 2 salmon. Release wild Chi- nook. Closed to fishing for or retaining steelhead. Aug. 1-Oct. 31 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6 salmon including no more than 2 adults. Release all salmon other than hatchery Chinook and hatchery coho. Closed to fishing for or retaining steelhead. Nov. 1-Mar. 31 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adult salmon or 2 hatchery steelhead or 1 of each. Release all salmon other than hatchery Chinook and hatchery coho.<br><b>from County Rd. Bridge below the former location of the powerhouse to 400’ below Big Brother Falls (river mile 16) CRC (508)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older). Selective gear rules, except barbed hooks are allowed.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Release wild cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Sat. before Memorial Day-July 31 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 2 salmon or 2 hatchery steelhead or 1 of each. Release all salmon other than hatchery salmon. Aug. 1-Oct. 31 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adult salmon or 2 hatchery steelhead or 1 of each. Release all salmon other than hatchery salmon.<br><b>from Big Brother Falls downstream 400’</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: CLOSED WATERS. Salmon and hatchery<br>• <b>steelhead</b>: (Continued on next column) (Continued on next page) SPECIES DATE ADDITIONAL RULES</details><br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.<br><br><i>Selective gear rules</i>: artificial flies or lures with barbless single-point hooks only, bait prohibited, up to 3 hooks, knotless nets only.",
