  parkRegsSrc:"washington",
  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 15 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>from Olympic National Park boundary upstream to Dept. of Natural Resource's Oxbow Campground boat launch CRC (350)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Closed September 1–15, 21, and 28; October 5 and 12. Only 1 single-point barbless hook allowed. Internal combustion motors prohibited. Jan. 1-Mar. 31 Bait prohibited. Apr. 1-May 31 Closed. June 1-Aug. 31 Bait prohibited. Sept. 1-Sept. 15 Closed.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: June 1-Aug. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout min. size 14\". Release wild rainbow trout. Sept. 16-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout min. size 14\". Release wild rainbow trout. Nov. 1-Mar. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Release cut- throat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: June 1-Aug. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Sept. 16-Mar. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Sept. 16-Nov. 30 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 3. Up to 2 adults including no more than 1 adult Chinook may be retained. Dec. 1-Dec. 15 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 1. Release all salmon other than coho.<br><b>from Dept. of Natural Resource's Oxbow Campground boat launch to Morgans Cross- ing boat launch CRC (348)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Only 1 single-point barbless hook allowed. Internal combustion motors prohibited. Apr. 1-May 31 Closed. June 1-Aug. 31 Bait prohibited. Sept. 1-Sept. 15 Closed. Sept. 16-Oct. 15 Bait prohibited. Dec. 1-Mar. 31 Bait prohibited. SPECIES DATE ADDITIONAL RULES<br>• <b>Trout</b>: June 1-Aug. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout min. size 14\". Release wild rainbow trout. Sept. 16-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout min. size 14\". Release wild rainbow trout. Nov. 1-Mar. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Release cut- throat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: June 1-Aug. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Sept. 16-Mar. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Oct. 16-Nov. 30 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 3. Up to 2 adults including no more than 1 adult Chinook may be retained. Dec. 1-Dec. 15 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 1. Release all salmon other than coho.<br><b>from Morgans Crossing boat launch site to Olympic National Park boundary below</b><br><b>mouth of South Fork Hoh CRC (348)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Fishing from any floating device prohibited. Only 1 single-point barbless hook allowed. Bait prohibited. Mar. 1-May 31 Closed. Sept. 1-Sept. 15 Closed.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: June 1-Aug. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout min. size 14\". Release wild rainbow trout. Sept. 16-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout min. size 14\". Release wild rainbow trout. Nov. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Release cut- throat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: June 1-Aug. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Sept. 16-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit.</details><br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.",
