  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 10 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>from mouth (Jessie Slough) to Hwy. 101 Bridge including all channels, sloughs, and interconnected waterways CRC (358)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Jan. 1-Last Day of Feb. Selective gear rules. Aug. 16-Aug. 31 Anti-snagging rule. Single-point barbless hooks required. Night closure. Sept. 1-Sept. 23 Closed. Sept. 24-Nov. 30 Single-point barbless hooks required. Anti-snagging rule. Night closure.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Aug. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\". Sept. 24-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\". Nov. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Release cut- throat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Aug. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Sept. 24-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Sept. 24-Oct. 15 Min. size 12\". Dailly limit 1. Release wild Chinook and wild coho. Oct. 16-Nov. 30 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adults. Release Chinook and wild coho. Dec. 1-Dec. 31 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 6 including no more than 1 adult. Release Chinook and wild coho.<br><b>from Hwy. 101 Bridge to confluence of East and West forks CRC (358)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Aug. 16-Aug. 31 Night closure. Single-point barbless hooks required. Sept. 1-Sept. 23 Closed. Sept. 24-Nov. 30 Single-point barbless hooks required. Night closure. Anti-snagging rule. Dec. 1-Last Day of Feb. Selective gear rules. Internal combustion motors prohibited. SPECIES DATE ADDITIONAL RULES<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Aug. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\". Sept. 24-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\". Nov. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Release cut- throat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Sept. 24-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Sept. 24-Oct. 15 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 1. Release wild Chinook and wild coho. Oct. 16-Nov. 30 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adults. Release Chinook and wild coho. Dec. 1-Dec. 31 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 6 including no more than 1 adult. Release Chinook and wild coho.</details><br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.<br><br><i>Selective gear rules</i>: artificial flies or lures with barbless single-point hooks only, bait prohibited, up to 3 hooks, knotless nets only.",
