  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 14 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>from mouth to bridge at Schafer State Park CRC (329)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Jan. 1-Mar. 31 Selective gear rules. Aug. 1-Sept. 30 Selective gear rules. Aug. 16-Nov. 30 Night closure. Oct. 1-Nov. 30 Single-point barbless hooks required.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\". Nov. 1-Mar. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Release cut- throat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Mar. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Oct. 1-Oct. 31 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adults. Release adult Chinook. Nov. 1-Dec. 31 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adults. Release Chinook.<br><b>from bridge at Schafer State Park upstream to 400' below Bingham Creek Hatchery dam CRC (329)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Aug. 16-Oct. 31 Single-point barbless hooks required. Night closure.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\".<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br><b>from 400' below Bingham Creek Hatchery dam to the dam CRC (329A)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Night closure. Open only to anglers with disabilities who permanently use a wheelchair and have a desig- nated harvester companion card. Jan. 1-Mar. 31 Selective gear rules. Aug. 16-Nov. 30 Single-point barbless hooks required.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\". Nov. 1-Mar. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Release cut- throat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Mar. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. SPECIES DATE ADDITIONAL RULES<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Oct. 1-Oct. 31 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adults. Release adult Chinook. Nov. 1-Dec. 31 Min. size 12\". Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adults. Release Chinook.</details><br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.<br><br><i>Selective gear rules</i>: artificial flies or lures with barbless single-point hooks only, bait prohibited, up to 3 hooks, knotless nets only.",
