/* ---------- Lakes ----------
   Still water, marked differently from rivers because it fishes differently
   and because a lake has no current to animate. Which lakes: the ones
   Yellowstone's own fishing regulations name. The park has 150-odd lakes
   and more than 40% of its waters were historically barren of fish, so
   "every lake" and "every fishable lake" are very different lists, and the
   regulations are the only source here that says which is which. `regs` is
   from that document. */
