  blurb:"Fifteen miles of water under the north end of the range, dammed in 1911 at the outlet of a natural lake. Marinas at Colter Bay and Leeks, a boat launch at Signal Mountain, and the only water in the park where a motor is much use.",
  fish:"Lake trout — big ones — along with Snake River fine-spotted cutthroat, brown trout and mountain whitefish. Deep, cold and moody: the fish are where the structure is, and in summer that is a long way down.",
  regs:"Park lakes are <b>open to fishing year-round</b>. <b>Jackson Lake closes October 1–31</b>, the one park lake with a closed season. Lake creel is <b>six trout</b>, no more than three of them cutthroat, and no more than one cutthroat over sixteen inches. The park publishes a <b>mercury consumption advisory</b> for fish from this lake. A <b>Wyoming fishing licence</b> is required — Grand Teton is fished under Wyoming regulations, not a park permit of its own.",
